These codes are just examples to guide through a simple concept on Contract Testing in unit tests. The actual implementation of such test depends on your project or project's design needs.

**ALSO NOTE:** Always keep in mind that contract tests are not meant to provide absolutely perfect coverage. They may fail tests randomly and that's just a possibility of the input being randomly generated.

For any professional software application testing, thorough manual testing must be conducted as well, because automated tests can't cover every possible edge case or every type of testing situation. 

