## Summary
A contract testing is a set of best practices where we verify the expected behaviors and the promises we make. In other words, these are our "contracts".

In this lesson, you learned about contract testing for ArrayList.IndexOf to prevent negative outcomes which violate the contract of the method.

This is beneficial because it makes testing and debugging much easier. Instead of blindly running tests trying not to break anything, we have a better understanding of our code and its behavior and can set preconditions accordingly.

For ArrayList.Count, you can similarly create a contract test to verify the behavior for this property too; i.e., its expected behavior and the promise made by the property.

In general, automated contract testing increases the confidence that code is following the expected contracts. These can prevent many more bugs from creeping in just by examining the behavior of data structures and algorithms.

Happy coding and testing with PEX and Contracts :smile:

